  "result": "## Summary\n\nI've added foreign currency support to `src/money.js`:\n\n**New exports:**\n\n1. **RATES** constant:\n   - `EUR: 1` (base rate)\n   - `USD: 1.085` (units of USD per EUR)\n   - `GBP: 0.8425` (units of GBP per EUR)\n\n2. **convert(cents, currency)**:\n   - Converts euro cents to target currency cents\n   - Applies exchange rate and rounds using banker's rounding\n   - Returns `ok(convertedCents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n\n3. **formatMoney(cents, currency)**:\n   - Formats amount in any supported currency\n   - Uses appropriate symbols: `\u20ac` for EUR, `$` for USD, `\u00a3` for GBP\n   - Falls back to currency code for unknown currencies\n   - Formats with thousands separators and 2 decimal places\n\n**New tests (17)** cover:\n- RATES structure and values\n- EUR to EUR, USD, GBP conversions\n- Error handling for unknown currencies\n- Negative amounts\n- Rounding behavior\n- Large amounts\n- Currency formatting for all supported currencies\n- Edge cases (zero, small amounts, negative amounts)\n- Combined convert + formatMoney workflow\n\nAll 284 tests pass (267 existing + 17 new).",
